# Code quality checks

Before marking work **done** (and before suggesting a commit), run this checklist on **changed and new** files. Fix issues in scope; do not drive-by fix unrelated legacy code.

Reference: [scholar-naming-conventions.mdc](./scholar-naming-conventions.mdc)

## Checklist (in order)

### 1. Naming

Read `.cursor/rules/scholar-naming-conventions.mdc` and verify:

- [ ] **Files & paths** — `snake_case`; spec suffix `_spec.rb`; partials lead with `_`
- [ ] **Classes / modules** — `PascalCase`; file path matches constant (autoload)
- [ ] **Methods, variables, params** — `snake_case`; predicates `?`; no camelCase
- [ ] **Rails roles** — singular models, plural controllers; `*Service`, `*Job`, `*Indexer` match project patterns
- [ ] **Work types** — 8 UC types unchanged unless PLAN explicitly consolidates (currently: keep all 8)

If a name is wrong, rename in the same slice (including spec paths and references).

### 2. Data integrity (when slice touches content)

- [ ] Run applicable checks from [INTEGRITY.md](docs/upgrade/INTEGRITY.md)
- [ ] Document count deltas in STATUS if not matching baseline

## Also run

After naming (and integrity when applicable):

- `bundle exec rubocop` on changed Ruby files
- `bin/rspec-fast` (or targeted paths); see [TESTING.md](docs/upgrade/TESTING.md)

Push for full CircleCI when ready.

## When to skip

- Question-only or read-only review: naming check on cited symbols only
- Legacy file touched for a one-line fix: do not rename unrelated identifiers in that file
